---
id: braised-cabbage-tomato-aromatics
title: Braised Cabbage with Tomato & Aromatics
category: modular_cooked_veg

yield:
  servings: 4
  cooked_g: 740

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Shred @green-cabbage{0.5%head} into 0.5 cm ribbons, discarding the hard central core. Finely dice @yellow-onion{0.66%onion}. Coarsely grate @carrots{100%g} on the large holes of a box grater.

Heat @olive-oil{2%tsp} in a wide, deep #skillet over medium heat. Add the diced onion and grated carrot. Sauté for ~saute-time{3.5%min} until the onions turn translucent and the carrot softens.

Add the shredded cabbage in batches, tossing frequently over medium-high heat for ~sear-time{4.5%min} until the leaves collapse by roughly a third and show light golden blistering on the edges.

Add @tomato-paste{2%tbsp}, @chicken-broth{100%ml}, @kosher-salt{1%tsp}, @black-pepper{0.5%tsp}, and @bay-leaves{2%leaf}. Stir vigorously for 30 seconds until the tomato paste dissolves into the simmering broth.

Turn the heat down to low, cover with a tight-fitting lid, and braise for ~braise-time{19%min}. Stir once at the halfway point to prevent scorching.

Remove the lid and discard the bay leaves. Increase the heat to medium for ~evaporate-time{2%min} to cook off loose puddle liquid so the rich tomato sauce glazes tightly onto the cabbage ribbons.

Divide equally into 4 meal prep containers (185 g cooked yield each) and let cool before sealing.
